## Dream Workflow Node Artifact Receipt

On 2026-06-09, Dream preflight execution moved behind the generic workflow-node seam. This supersedes the earlier core-wired `DreamMemoryFabricPort` path.

Decision:

- Dreaming is a workflow cartridge/package, not a runner feature.
- Workflow cartridges/capsules are Cloudflare artifact-backed data: manifests, generated machine configs, generated harness/source, package exports, contracts, hashes, and receipts can all live in Artifacts and be validated before execution.
- Code-like exports inside a cartridge are still artifacts. They need entitlement, version pinning, hash verification, package/export contract checks, capability leases for side effects, and execution receipts.
- The runner executes generated `workflow.node.invoke` states through a generic `WorkflowNodeAdapterPort`; it does not switch on Dream vocabulary.
- Dream owns `joelclaw.dream.source-inventory`, `joelclaw.dream.source-health`, `joelclaw.dream.backfill-plan`, `joelclaw.dream.memory-search`, `joelclaw.dream.hydrate`, `joelclaw.dream.correlate`, and `joelclaw.dream.hitl-report` node types behind `src/app/workflow-nodes/dream-memory-fabric.ts`.

Changed surfaces:

- `src/app/application/ports.ts` defines the generic `WorkflowNodeAdapterPort`, `WorkflowNodeInvocationStep`, and `WorkflowNodeExecutionResult`.
- `src/app/application/workflow-app.ts` no longer imports Dream schemas, Dream ports, Dream step kinds, or Dream execution helpers.
- `src/app/domain/schemas.ts` no longer admits `dream.source-inventory`, `dream.source-health`, or `dream.backfill-plan` as core dynamic workflow step kinds and no longer owns Dream document schemas.
- Generated Dream preflight steps now appear as `workflow.node.invoke` with package-style `nodeType`, `config`, `packageRefs`, `inputRefs`, dependencies, and output path.
- Missing node adapter still blocks with `adapter_unavailable`; adapterless workflow cartridge work is not treated as completed work.
- `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-workflow-front-door.ts` accepts an optional `workflowNodeAdapter`, not a Dream-specific dependency.
- `src/app/infrastructure/memory-adapters.ts` includes an integration-test Dream memory fabric adapter that emits honest local fixture coverage: native Pi/Codex/Cloudflare, missing Claude, degraded health, and recovery-only backfill.
- `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-dream-memory-fabric-relay.ts` adds the Cloudflare-facing HTTP relay adapter. It posts to `/memory/inventory`, `/memory/source-health`, `/memory/backfill/plan`, `/memory/search`, and `/memory/hydrate` with a secret-backed bearer token, parses typed Dream documents, and returns typed blockers on secret or relay failures.
- `src/app/index.ts` exports the Dream node adapter and Cloudflare-facing relay adapter factory/types as package/plugin-facing surfaces; it does not export trusted local filesystem relay cartridges.

Validation receipts:

