## Trusted Dream Memory Relay Contract Receipt

On 2026-06-09, the Dream memory relay boundary gained typed request/response contracts for the full retrieval loop, not just the first preflight calls.

Decision:

- Cloudflare talks to the memory fabric through `dream.memory-relay.request.v1`, not direct local paths, raw transcript stores, or Typesense credentials.
- Every relay request carries actor, scope, allowed source families, purpose, budget, time window, redaction policy, idempotency key, lease ref, trace context, run id, and work item id.
- Every relay response carries `dream.memory-relay.response.v1`, operation id, lease receipt, missing sources, source freshness, source inventory refs, follow-up links, and a typed document payload.
- The full relay endpoint catalog is now explicit: `/memory/inventory`, `/memory/search`, `/memory/signals`, `/memory/hydrate`, `/memory/correlate`, `/memory/backfill/plan`, `/memory/backfill/run`, `/memory/capture/run`, `/memory/capture/artifact`, and `/memory/source-health`.
- Dream retrieval artifacts now have Zod contracts for search hits, signals, hydration, correlation graph, backfill execution receipts, and capture receipts.
- Existing Cloudflare relay client calls for inventory/source-health/backfill-plan/search/hydrate/correlate now wrap payloads in the relay request envelope and require the response envelope before accepting documents.

Changed surfaces:

- `src/app/workflow-nodes/dream-memory-fabric-schemas.ts` now defines:
  - `dream.memory-relay.request.v1`
  - `dream.memory-relay.response.v1`
  - `dream.memory-relay.endpoint-catalog.v1`
  - `dream.memory-search.v1`
  - `dream.signals.v1`
  - `dream.hydration.v1`
  - `dream.correlation-graph.v1`
  - `dream.backfill-run-receipt.v1`
  - `dream.capture-receipt.v1`
- `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-dream-memory-fabric-relay.ts` publishes `dreamMemoryRelayEndpointCatalog` and posts typed envelopes with redacted lease/trace/idempotency metadata.
- `src/app/index.ts` exports the relay schemas, inferred types, response-envelope helper, and endpoint catalog.
- `tests/integration/dream-memory-fabric-contract.test.ts` covers the full relay document contract.
- `tests/integration/cloudflare-dream-memory-fabric-relay.test.ts` proves Cloudflare sends envelope-shaped requests, does not leak the relay token, accepts only response-envelope documents, and exposes the full endpoint catalog.

