## Trusted Local Dream Memory Fabric Adapter Receipt

On 2026-06-09, the trusted relay side gained its first non-fixture memory-fabric adapter for local authority roots.

Decision:

- `createTrustedLocalDreamMemoryFabricAdapter` implements `DreamMemoryFabricPort` for trusted local/NAS-style filesystem roots.
- This adapter belongs to the Dream workflow cartridge under `src/cartridges/dream-memory-fabric/`, behind the relay server, not in the Cloudflare Worker bundle or core app barrel. It imports `node:fs/promises`, owns raw private paths, and returns only redacted locators plus hashes/counts/freshness.
- Configured source roots carry `sourceId`, family, privacy tier, optional runtime, authority root, extension filters, and optional derived-index roots or counts.
- Authority roots are source of truth. Derived QMD/Typesense/view/vector/SQLite indexes are freshness-checked outputs.
- The adapter emits `dream.source-inventory.v1`, `dream.source-health.v1`, and `dream.backfill-plan.v1` through the same schemas Cloudflare already expects.
- Missing or stale derived indexes become recovery-only backfill actions. Missing runtime-native capture becomes a capture fix. This keeps backfill as repair, not normal operation.
- Dream remains a workflow cartridge/node set. This adapter is one installed relay capability, not a Dream-specific runner branch.

Changed surfaces:

- `src/cartridges/dream-memory-fabric/trusted-local-memory-fabric.ts` adds the trusted local adapter.
- `src/app/index.ts` intentionally does not export the local Dream adapter; cartridge callers import from the cartridge/package surface.
- `tests/integration/trusted-local-dream-memory-fabric.test.ts` creates temporary Pi, Codex, Brain, and Cloudflare roots; proves redacted inventory; proves no raw authority paths leak; proves Codex/Pi/Cloudflare runtime coverage comes from native roots; proves Claude missing coverage is explicit; and proves stale/missing derived indexes produce recovery backfill actions.

