## Trusted Local Dream Relay Real Source Proof

On 2026-06-09, the trusted local Dream relay was exercised against real local authority roots instead of fixture roots.

Decision:

- Local operator source-root config belongs under ignored operational state, not Brain. The active raw-path config is `.wrangler/workflow-app/dream-relay/source-roots.json`.
- Docs/pdf-brain access is an optional trusted relay adapter, not a direct Worker scrape and not a local path assumption. The proof harness defaults to the public-read JoelClaw docs API discovery/search/chunk surface through `DREAM_DOCS_API_BASE_URL`.
- Dream memory search is now family-balanced after each adapter ranks its own hits. This prevents docs/pdf-brain, transcripts, Brain, or Cloudflare run receipts from monopolizing a Dream just because one source returns larger numeric scores.
- The repeatable proof command is `pnpm app:dream:relay:proof`.
- The proof starts the trusted relay on an ephemeral localhost port with a generated bearer token, calls authenticated `/healthz`, then drives `inventory`, `source-health`, `backfill-plan`, `search`, `hydrate`, and `correlate` through the same HTTP relay contract Cloudflare uses.
- The proof writes only a redacted receipt to `.wrangler/workflow-app/dream-relay/latest-local-proof.json`; it does not write raw source roots, bearer tokens, or transcript bodies to Brain.

