## Dream Search And Hydration Cartridge Node Receipt

On 2026-06-09, Dream's generated workflow language gained package-backed search and hydration nodes.

Decision:

- T-shaped Dreaming cannot stop at inventory/health/backfill planning. Generated workflows need explicit retrieval nodes before report assembly.
- `DreamMemoryRetrievalPort` now lives with the Dream workflow-node contract, next to `DreamMemoryFabricPort`, so infrastructure and cartridges implement ports instead of owning domain contracts.
- `joelclaw.dream.memory-search` writes `dream.memory-search.v1` from a relay-backed search payload.
- `joelclaw.dream.hydrate` reads a prior search artifact, selects bounded unique receipt refs, and writes `dream.hydration.v1` with redacted evidence. It blocks if no search artifact or receipts exist.
- The Cloudflare relay adapter now implements both `DreamMemoryFabricPort` and `DreamMemoryRetrievalPort`; the Dream Cloudflare installer wires the same secret-backed relay adapter into both ports when `DREAM_MEMORY_RELAY_BASE_URL` is configured.
- `createArtifactBackedWorkflowCartridgeAdapter` now continues across multiple pinned package refs when an earlier package does not export the requested node. This matters once workflows compose multiple cartridges.

