## Dream Generated Workflow Proof Receipt

On 2026-06-09, Dream gained an explicit generated-workflow proof contract and a generic post-execution artifact recorder path.

Decision:

- `dream.generated-workflow-proof.v1` is the cartridge-owned proof document for a Dream run's generated plan/machine/harness/execution chain.
- The proof verifies the pinned dynamic plan hash, generated XState config hash, generated XState TypeScript source hash, generated harness source hash, Dream package ref, source-profile effect coverage, machine step order, execution completed step ids, generated state sequence, planner prompt ref, and planner transcript ref.
- The proof fails if a workflow tries to pass generic legacy step kinds such as `research.review`, `capability.discord.message`, or `review.summary` off as a Dream generated workflow.
- The Dream integration helper no longer appends the old generic research/Discord/review suffix after the Dream package nodes. A Dream preflight chain is now seven Dream cartridge nodes: source inventory, source health, backfill plan, memory search, hydration, correlation graph, and HITL report.
- The runner now has a generic `WorkflowPostExecutionArtifactRecorderPort`. Dream proof capture is one installed recorder, not Dream logic inside the core workflow runner.
- The Dream recorder writes `dream/generated-workflow-proof.json` after `workflow.execution-proof.v1`; the resulting artifact ref flows into receipt refs, review-gate step artifact refs, captured artifact refs, and review-surface inputs.
- The installed-cartridge registry installs the Dream proof recorder only when the relay-backed Dream cartridge adapter is installed through the Dream cartridge's `DREAM_MEMORY_RELAY_BASE_URL` binding.
- This is still a local/integration proof when the execution proof status is `not-proven-local-integration`; it does not claim live Cloudflare execution.

Changed surfaces:

- `src/app/application/ports.ts` adds `WorkflowPostExecutionArtifactRecorderPort`.
- `src/app/application/workflow-app.ts` records optional post-execution artifacts after execution proof capture and before review summary/surface publication.
- `src/app/workflow-nodes/dream-memory-fabric-schemas.ts` now owns `DreamMemoryFabricNodeTypeSchema`, `DreamWorkflowEffectSchema`, and `DreamGeneratedWorkflowProofDocumentSchema`.
- `src/app/workflow-nodes/dream-generated-workflow-proof.ts` adds `verifyDreamGeneratedWorkflow`, a pure verifier over pinned plan, generated machine, machine source, harness source, execution proof, and expected Dream package ref, plus `createDreamGeneratedWorkflowProofRecorder`.
- `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-workflow-front-door.ts` supports run-store-scoped post-execution recorder factories.
- `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-worker-route.ts` installs the Dream generated-workflow proof recorder alongside the Dream cartridge adapter when the trusted relay is configured.
- `tests/integration/workflow-app.test.ts` now proves Dream runs are package-backed Dream-effect workflows and reads the redacted generated workflow proof document from `result.artifactRefs`; the test no longer writes the proof manually.
- `tests/integration/workflow-app.test.ts` also proves the verifier rejects the generic research/Discord/review chain as failed Dream proof instead of letting it masquerade as Dreaming.
- `tests/integration/cloudflare-worker-route.test.ts` proves relay config installs both the Dream cartridge adapter and Dream proof recorder.

