## Workflow Cartridge Composite Adapter Receipt

On 2026-06-09, the installed-cartridge dependency combiner stopped enforcing a single workflow-node adapter.

Decision:

- Multiple installed cartridges may contribute `WorkflowNodeAdapterPort` factories.
- The core installer composes those adapters generically instead of forcing callers to write a Dream-specific or one-off composite.
- `adapter_unavailable` means "try the next installed cartridge adapter."
- Any non-availability blocker, such as `stale_package`, remains authoritative and stops dispatch. A bad package/export/hash/lease must not be masked by another adapter.
- Post-execution artifact recorder factories are still aggregated across installed cartridges.

Why this matters:

- Dream is no longer the only shape the Worker composition can realistically support.
- Future workflow packages can install their own node adapters without changing the core runner or adding `if`/`switch` branches.
- The current compiled cartridge registry is still temporary, but it now behaves like an additive plugin registry instead of a single-cartridge slot.

Changed surfaces:

- `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-workflow-cartridge-installer.ts` now builds a composite `WorkflowNodeAdapterPort` when more than one installed cartridge contributes an adapter.
- `tests/integration/cloudflare-workflow-cartridge-installer.test.ts` proves composite dispatch tries the second adapter after `adapter_unavailable`, preserves `stale_package` from a matching adapter, and aggregates post-execution recorders.

Validation receipts:

- `pnpm vitest run tests/integration/cloudflare-workflow-cartridge-installer.test.ts tests/integration/cloudflare-worker-route.test.ts` passed: `2` files, `23` tests.
