- `pnpm typecheck` passed.
- `pnpm typecheck:tsc` passed.

## Dream Wzrrd Primary Document Receipt

On 2026-06-09, Dream output moved closer to the actual requested Wzrrd report shape.

Decision:

- A Wzrrd run can now carry an optional `outputTarget.primaryDocument` that points at a redacted text artifact produced by the generated workflow.
- `wzrrd.publish-payload.v1` pins that primary document by artifact ref, SHA-256 text hash, media type, publish path, and title.
- The Wzrrd publisher verifies the primary document hash before publication. If present, it publishes a static `index.html` preview from the primary document, the canonical source file at the requested path, and `review-surface.json`.
- Dream HITL reports now write both `dream/hitl-report.json` and sibling `dream/hitl-report.mdsvx`. The JSON remains the typed machine contract and first output ref; the MDSvX artifact is the publishable report source.
- The real planner prompt now tells Pi planners to set `outputTarget.primaryDocument` when a generated workflow renders a public report. For Dream HITL reports, the intended artifact path is `dream/hitl-report.mdsvx` and publish path is `report.mdsvx`.
- This is still not a full SvelteKit/MDSvX build inside the Worker. The current Cloudflare Wzrrd API adapter publishes static files. The source artifact and static preview are now explicit, but a future Wzrrd/template adapter should compile the Tufte/MDSvX report before publication.

Changed surfaces:

- `src/app/domain/schemas.ts` adds `outputTarget.primaryDocument` for Wzrrd targets and `primaryDocument` for `wzrrd.publish-payload.v1`.
- `src/app/workflow-nodes/dream-memory-fabric.ts` writes a sibling `text/mdsvx` artifact for `joelclaw.dream.hitl-report`.
- `src/app/application/workflow-app.ts` resolves and hashes the generated primary document before requesting a Wzrrd publish lease.
- `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-wzrrd-publish-adapter.ts` verifies and publishes the primary document alongside `review-surface.json`.
- `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-agent-lane-adapters.ts` documents the planner contract for primary Wzrrd documents.
- `tests/integration/workflow-app.test.ts` proves the generated Dream workflow emits `dream/hitl-report.mdsvx` and pins it into the Wzrrd payload.
- `tests/integration/cloudflare-wzrrd-publish-adapter.test.ts` proves the real Wzrrd adapter publishes `index.html`, `report.mdsvx`, and `review-surface.json` from a verified primary document.

Validation receipts:

- `pnpm vitest run tests/integration/workflow-app.test.ts tests/integration/cloudflare-wzrrd-publish-adapter.test.ts tests/integration/dream-memory-fabric-contract.test.ts` passed: `3` files, `34` tests.
- `pnpm test:integration` passed: `29` files, `135` tests.
- `pnpm typecheck` passed.
