## Dream Wzrrd Renderer Port Receipt

On 2026-06-09, the Wzrrd primary-document preview stopped being a hardwired source dump.

Decision:

- Wzrrd publishing remains the leased side-effect adapter. It verifies the publish payload, review surface hash, primary document hash, review approval, leased slug, and Wzrrd API token.
- Report rendering is now a package-style seam: `primaryDocumentRenderer` receives the hash-pinned primary document, publish payload, and review surface and returns static files such as `index.html` and supporting assets.
- The default renderer is `joel/static-tufte-mdsvx-preview@0.1.0`. It renders a safe Tufte-ish static preview for `text/mdsvx`/markdown, strips frontmatter, renders headings/lists/prose/code, shows fenced `d2` as a workflow-state-machine figure source, and publishes the canonical report source unchanged beside `review-surface.json`.
- This is still intentionally not a full SvelteKit/MDSvX/D2 compiler inside the Worker. The renderer id and docs say that plainly. A future `@joelhooks/wzrrd-hitl-report` package can replace the renderer while `wzrrd.site.publish` continues to own only publication.

Changed surfaces:

- `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-wzrrd-publish-adapter.ts` adds `WzrrdPrimaryDocumentRenderer`, `WzrrdPrimaryDocumentRenderInput`, `WzrrdPrimaryDocumentRenderResult`, `WzrrdPublishFile`, and `createStaticTufteMdsvxPrimaryDocumentRenderer`.
- `src/app/index.ts` exports the renderer seam for package/plugin composition.
- `tests/integration/cloudflare-wzrrd-publish-adapter.test.ts` proves the default renderer renders a real static preview and that an injected package-style renderer can own `index.html` and assets while the publisher still publishes the canonical `report.mdsvx` and `review-surface.json`.
- `docs/dream-report-canon.md` now records the split between `wzrrd.report.render` and `wzrrd.site.publish`.

