## Dream Backfill Run Node Receipt

On 2026-06-09, Dream recovery backfill moved from "planned only" to an executable workflow-node receipt.

Decision:

- `joelclaw.dream.backfill-run` is a Dream cartridge node, not core runner logic.
- The generated Dream sequence is now source inventory -> source health -> backfill plan -> backfill run receipt -> memory search -> redacted hydration -> correlation graph -> HITL report.
- `DreamMemoryBackfillPort` is separate from source inventory/health planning. A trusted adapter may execute controlled recovery work, but if no writer is registered it must emit `skipped` or `blocked` action results instead of claiming fake indexed rows.
- The HITL report now consumes both the recovery plan and the recovery run receipt. The report source refs prove what was planned and what was actually attempted.
- The relay contract now treats `/memory/backfill/run` as a supported operation for Cloudflare, trusted server, trusted-local HTTP relay, live preflight readiness, local proof, and provisioning preflight.

Changed surfaces:

- `src/app/workflow-nodes/dream-memory-fabric-schemas.ts` adds the `joelclaw.dream.backfill-run` node type and `DreamMemoryRelayBackfillRunPayloadSchema`.
- `src/app/workflow-nodes/dream-memory-fabric.ts` adds `DreamMemoryBackfillPort`, executes `joelclaw.dream.backfill-run`, loads the run receipt in `joelclaw.dream.hitl-report`, and renders the backfill-run state in the D2 proof.
- `src/app/infrastructure/cloudflare-dream-memory-fabric-relay.ts` implements relay-backed `runBackfill` through `/memory/backfill/run`.
- `src/app/infrastructure/trusted-dream-memory-relay-server.ts` dispatches `backfill-run` and returns `dream.backfill-run-receipt.v1` envelopes.
- `src/cartridges/dream-memory-fabric/trusted-local-memory-fabric.ts` implements the trusted-local backfill port honestly: no controlled writer means `skipped`; unavailable authority means `blocked`.
- `src/cartridges/dream-memory-fabric/trusted-local-relay-http.ts` advertises `backfill-run` in authenticated `/healthz`.
- `src/cartridges/dream-memory-fabric/package-seed.ts` exports eight Dream workflow nodes, including `joelclaw.dream.backfill-run`.

