## Dream Relay Capability Preflight Receipt

On 2026-06-10, live Dream preflight started emitting a typed, redacted `relayCapability` contract instead of leaving the relay lease hidden in prose.

Decision:

- `workflow.live-preflight.v1` now includes the exact relay capability envelope Cloudflare is allowed to use: `dream.memory.relay`.
- The envelope records allowed operations (`inventory`, `source-health`, `backfill-plan`, `backfill-run`, `search`, `hydrate`, `correlate`), allowed source families, budget defaults, idempotency prefix, lease secret binding name, non-secret `secretRef`, readiness booleans/statuses, and the relay redaction policy.
- `workflow.dream-live-run-request.v1` copies the preflight `relayCapability` into blocked/prepared/submitted run receipts. A Dream request can now prove which relay capability it depended on even when submission is refused.
- This is not network exposure. The latest receipt still says endpoint configured `false`, token configured `false`, Worker base URL configured `false`, healthz `missing`, local proof `passed`.

Changed surfaces:

- `src/app/domain/schemas.ts` adds `WorkflowLivePreflightRelayCapabilitySchema` and includes it in live preflight and Dream run request receipts.
- `scripts/workflow-app-dream-preflight.ts` builds the redacted capability contract from current checks, Worker config text, env/remote secret inventory, and fixed Dream relay envelope constraints.
- `scripts/workflow-app-dream-run.ts` carries the validated preflight relay capability into the run request receipt.
- `tests/integration/dream-live-preflight.test.ts` and `tests/integration/dream-live-run-request.test.ts` assert no relay token leak and require the capability contract in ready/blocked receipts.

