## Dream Refinement Proposal Node Receipt

On 2026-06-10, the Dream workflow gained a refinement-loop node without baking Dream into the core runner.

Decision:

- `joelclaw.dream.refinement-proposals` is a workflow cartridge node exported by `workflow/dream-memory-fabric`, not a core app branch.
- The generated Dream workflow must invoke the needed cartridge nodes through the generated machine; refinement proposals are a verifier-required effect for current Dream runs, not proof that the runner owns a fixed Dream sequence.
- The node writes `dream.refinement-proposals.v1` to `dream/refinement-proposals.json`.
- The proposal artifact is the next-workflow seed: it captures actionable kernel/package/workflow/schema/capability/capture-ingest improvements with concise summary, reasoning, rating, recommendation, next step, and receipt metadata.
- The HITL report consumes the proposal artifact and surfaces the proposal count/ref/source refs, so the Dream report starts with dreams/work-to-do and keeps proof below.
- The generated workflow proof and live run request now require the proposal artifact alongside planner transcript, generated XState config, generated harness source, hashes, execution proof, per-node invocation proofs, HITL report, and Wzrrd publish receipt.

Changed surfaces:

- `src/app/workflow-nodes/dream-memory-fabric-schemas.ts` defines `DreamRefinementProposalDocumentSchema` and adds the refinement node type.
- `src/app/workflow-nodes/dream-memory-fabric.ts` executes the refinement node, writes `dream/refinement-proposals.json`, feeds proposals into the report node, and includes the refinement state in the D2 machine diagram.
- `src/cartridges/dream-memory-fabric/package-seed.ts` exports `contract://workflow/dream-memory-fabric/refinement-proposals.v1`.
- `scripts/workflow-app-dream-preflight.ts` and `scripts/workflow-app-dream-run.ts` require the refinement artifact/node in live readiness and blocked run receipts.
- `tests/integration/workflow-app.test.ts`, `tests/integration/dream-memory-fabric-contract.test.ts`, `tests/integration/dream-live-preflight.test.ts`, and `tests/integration/dream-live-run-request.test.ts` cover the proposal artifact, report integration, package proof, and live request shape.

