## Dream Live Run Fresh Preflight Receipt

On 2026-06-10, the Dream live-run harness stopped trusting stale preflight receipts for submit attempts.

Decision:

- `pnpm app:dream:run --submit` refreshes `workflow.live-preflight.v1` in the same process before it decides whether to call `POST /runs`.
- The run receipt records `preflight.refreshed` and the refreshed preflight `generatedAt` timestamp.
- `--skip-preflight-refresh` exists for offline fixture tests and manual receipt inspection, but it should not be used to claim live readiness.
- This is a non-exposure readiness fix. It does not create a tunnel, set relay URL/token, or expose JoelClaw/Typesense over a new network boundary.

Changed surfaces:

- `scripts/workflow-app-dream-run.ts` imports `runDreamPreflightCli`, refreshes preflight by default for `--submit`, passes `--allow-missing` so blocked receipts still get written, and refuses submission unless the refreshed receipt is ready.
- `src/app/domain/schemas.ts` adds `preflight.refreshed` and optional `preflight.generatedAt` to `workflow.dream-live-run-request.v1`.
- `tests/integration/dream-live-run-request.test.ts` proves a stale ready preflight on disk cannot submit when the same invocation refreshes to a blocked preflight.

