## Dream Relay Exact Sign-Off Gate Receipt

On 2026-06-10, the Dream relay provisioning preflight stopped treating an approval reference as owner sign-off.

Decision:

- `approvalRef` is provenance only. It can point to where approval was recorded, but it cannot by itself approve relay exposure.
- `approvalSignoff` must exactly equal `exposing JoelClaw/Typesense over a new network boundary` for the receipt to report `approval.status=approved`.
- Non-matching sign-off text reports `approval.status=invalid`.
- Missing sign-off text reports `approval.status=required`.
- The preflight remains non-mutating. It does not start tunnels, create funnels, rotate secrets, edit Worker config, set Worker vars, deploy, or expose the relay.

Changed surfaces:

- `scripts/workflow-app-dream-relay-provisioning-preflight.ts` now parses `--approval-signoff`, records `approval.signoffProvided`, and only reaches `ready-for-approved-provisioning` with the exact phrase.
- `tests/integration/dream-relay-provisioning-preflight.test.ts` covers missing sign-off, `approvalRef` without sign-off, invalid sign-off, exact sign-off, missing local proof, stale proof, and missing machine coverage.

